==={{OoA|-}} (Himekawa)===
{{Noncanon|Start}}
In the {{OoA (Himekawa)}}, Deer first appear after Link and [[Impa]] enter the forest [[Nayru]] is hiding in. Alongside the other animals, they aggressively confront the two, demanding they go back.<ref>{{Cite Book|quote= Go back. Go back. Go back.|book= {{OoA (Himekawa)|-}}|publisher= VIZ Media|page= 22}}</ref> Since he was able to speak with animals in [[Holodrum]],<ref>{{Cite Book|quote= In Holodrum I could speak with animals... Maybe I still can.|book= {{OoA (Himekawa)|-}}|publisher= VIZ Media|page= 22}}</ref> Link tells the forest dwellers they mean no harm and that [[Princess Zelda]] sent them to find Nayru.<ref>{{Cite Book|quote= We mean no harm. Princess Zelda sent us here to find Nayru.|book= {{OoA (Himekawa)|-}}|publisher= VIZ Media|page= 23}}</ref> The Deer and animals are surprised Link can speak to them, realizing he is a [[Hylian]] of the old blood.<ref>{{Cite Book|quote= He can speak to us. His ears are pointed. He's a Hylian. A Hylian of the old blood!|book= {{OoA (Himekawa)|-}}|publisher= VIZ Media|page= 23}}</ref> Meanwhile, Nayru stops strumming the [[Harp of Ages]] in her glade. A doe stands nearby and asks Nayru with the smaller animals around her to continue singing.<ref>{{Cite Book|quote= What's wrong, Nayru? Sing some more. Please?|book= {{OoA (Himekawa)|-}}|publisher= VIZ Media|page= 24}}</ref> The doe watches as Link and Impa converse with the oracle. When Impa is revealed to be possessed by [[Veran]],<ref>{{Cite Book|quote= I'm not Impa! My name is Veran!!|book= {{OoA (Himekawa)|-}}|publisher= VIZ Media|page= 27}}</ref> the doe leads a charge against the [[Sheikah]] to protect Nayru. However, once the doe and other animals make contact with Impa, Veran leaves her host and possesses Nayru instead.<ref>{{Cite Book|quote= You possessed Impa then jumped to Nayru?!|book= {{OoA (Himekawa)|-}}|publisher= VIZ Media|page= 29}}</ref> Veran enters [[Labrynna]]'s past using Nayru, leaving the Harp of Ages behind.<ref>{{Cite Book|quote= All that's left...Is this Harp.|book= {{OoA (Himekawa)|-}}|publisher= VIZ Media|page= 41}}</ref> The doe spectates as Link and [[Ralph]] fight over the Harp before Link accidentally strums it and is transported to the past.
{{Noncanon|End}}

